[17.161522, "o", "    - rbac.roles.agent.permissions.properties.conditions.field"]
[17.161657, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.161768, "o", "      this rule only shows rows of \"properties\" where \"agent_id\" equals the id of the user who is logged in — but \"agent_id\" holds the id of a row in \"agents\", which is a different kind of id. As written the rule matches NO rows, ever, and nothing reports an error: the app just shows nothing."]
[17.162027, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.162163, "o", "      → give \"agents\" a column that stores the login id (call it \"user_id\" and mark it unique), point \"agent_id\" at it with \"references\": \"user_id\", and fill it in for the rows that already exist. If \"agent_id\" already holds login ids, this warning does not apply."]
[17.162335, "o", "\r\n"]
